  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nDuring a commercial-driver review after a refrigerated-freight run, the nurse brings together the driver's account, a dated clinical attachment and an employer form copied from an earlier assessment; the documents refer to different times, and the current entry distinguishes a completed examination from recollections, plans and information concerning another person.\n\nThe current clinician's recorded hearing assessment finds no hearing loss after examining the driver in suitable conditions, although yesterday's radio conversation was difficult when the cab speaker crackled and the windows were open; a colleague who uses hearing aids is mentioned in the same discussion, but those aids belong to the colleague, and an undated employer checklist is not used to replace today's completed clinical assessment.\n\nThe driver alternates urban deliveries with a longer motorway leg and describes a busy depot where engine noise, glare and interrupted meals can complicate an account of symptoms; the nurse records the work setting as context, while keeping the dated clinical findings distinct from the driver's explanation for why a symptom might have occurred on that shift.\n\nBefore closing the interview, the nurse checks that the driver's recollection and the supplied clinical document have not been merged into a single undated finding, and records the outstanding documents separately; the completed entries remain current findings, while any missing qualification, conflicting detail or unperformed examination stays available for review rather than being silently treated as normal.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
